# Python standards (docpii)

## DRY and structure

- Reuse `src/docpii/` before adding logic in scripts or tests.
- Extract repeated patterns once; avoid copy-paste across modules.
- Prefer extending existing functions/classes over parallel implementations.

## Documentation

- Google-style docstrings on all public functions and classes (`Args`, `Returns`).
- Type hints on all parameters and return types (`X | None`, not bare `Optional` unless existing file uses it).

## Coupling

- Keep inter-module dependencies shallow: `schemas` → `templates` → `inference` / `evaluation` / `data`.
- Scripts must not import from each other; both scripts and CLI import from `docpii`.
- Avoid circular imports; use local imports only when breaking a cycle.

## Quality

- `ruff` (line length 100), `pytest` for behavior that matters.
- Specific exceptions; `logging.exception()` on failures in library code.
